    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d987">

                <pb facs="0667" n="595" sameAs="frus:frus1865p4/pg595"/>

                <head>Grutli Union of Schönenberg</head>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>Schönenberg</placeName>, <date
                        ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-volume-rules" calendar="gregorian"
                        notAfter="1865-07-31T23:59:59+00:34" notBefore="1865-04-15T00:00:00+00:34"
                        >undated</date>
                </dateline>
                <note rend="inline" rendition="#center" type="source">[Translation.]</note>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: All the members of the Grutli-Union, of
                    Schönenberg, twenty-six in number, congratulate the brave North in their recent
                    victories for freedom and humanity in the United States. They also deeply
                    deplore the death of President Lincoln, and hope that God will now give the
                    country a permanent peace.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>JOHN GURTLER, <hi rendition="#italic">President</hi>.</item>
                            <item>ED. ULRICH, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary</hi>.</item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
